    "narrative": "For Ghost Ride the WHIP on August 24, our priority is aggressively attacking the stolen base category, making **Corbin Carroll** (74.65) and **Seiya Suzuki** (72.23) our primary engines. **Corbin Carroll** is the standout play today; while facing a respectable arm in Kevin Gausman, his 86th percentile SB projection combined with a favorable #2 order slot and a +4% boost for Gausman\u2019s slow delivery to the plate makes him our highest-upside asset. Similarly, **Seiya Suzuki** benefits from a strong +19% SP skill adjustment against Merrill Kelly, cementing his status as a lock in the outfield. While **Mickey Moniak** (60.19) and **Max Muncy** (61.65) remain in the lineup as solid starters, both occupy the fringes of our rotation, providing utility in deep leagues but requiring consistent output to justify their slots over more high-variance options.\n\nThe most challenging decision today involved **Cole Young** (31.76), who fell well short of our starting threshold. While we value his versatility, the combination of a daunting matchup against Zack Wheeler and an unfavorable #7 batting position made him an easy exclusion. Conversely, **Zach McKinstry** (40.85) barely held onto his spot, saved only by a +5% park factor and wind conditions that lean in his favor; he remains the first candidate for mid-game substitution if his early at-bats prove unproductive. We are also navigating caution with **Gabriel Moreno** and **Josh Naylor**, both of whom are facing high-level arms in Gausman and Wheeler respectively. **Josh Naylor**\u2019s score is suppressed significantly by Wheeler\u2019s elite 3.06 xERA, but we are running him out there to maintain our power footprint. We continue to monitor the status of **Brice Turang** and **Jose Caballero**, who are sidelined today due to scheduling, forcing us to lean heavily on the remaining active roster to keep our 5x5 pace steady.",
